{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — the sense of \"and He will not condemn him\": that HaShem will show the righteousness of the righteous. He mentioned this because a wicked man, if he cannot in his jealousy kill him, will seek a pretext against the righteous — that he gave him money, or that the righteous did violence to him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:01.658410228Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}